Are stethoscopes common where you're playing?  Because they are _major_
game enhancement tools if you know how to use them.  I'm talking about
always knowing exactly how many hit points your opponent has left,
so you can make an educated decision about whether to run away or get
in that last fatal blow.  I'm talking about being able to pick off your
weakest opponent first when surrounded, thereby reducing their numbers
as quickly as possible.  It's nice to be able to detect secret doors
on the first try all the time, too.  Once you've played a healer for a
while, it's hard to imagine how you ever got along without a stethoscope.
(Also, because you start the game with 4 potions of healing and 4 potions
of extra healing, you get a minimum of 12 and a maximum of 24 additional
hit points at first level.)

